※ A tuple is a run of members and not a shape, so there is one place to name and
※ one index to name it with.  An array is what takes one index per dimension.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let p: 〈u8, u8〉 = 〈1u8, 2u8〉
    p⟦0,1⟧
